{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added per-feed `fetch_timeout` (integer seconds, 0 = use the global timeout).\n\n- Migration: new `feeds.fetch_timeout int not null default 0` column.\n- Model: `Feed.FetchTimeout` (`json:\"fetch_timeout\"`), `FeedModificationRequest.FetchTimeout`, applied in `Patch`; new `Feed.EffectiveFetchTimeout(global)` helper.\n- Storage: the column is read in the feed query builder and written in `UpdateFeed`.\n- Refresh: `RefreshFeed` now passes the per-feed timeout to the request builder, falling back to the global one when it is 0.\n- Validation: `PUT /v1/feeds/{feedID}` rejects a negative `fetch_timeout`.\n- Go client: `fetch_timeout` added to `Feed` and `FeedModificationRequest`.\n\nExisting unit and integration tests pass; nothing exercises the new behaviour yet.\n\nNot covered:\n- The override applies only to the feed refresh request. Icon fetches, the entry scraper and feed creation still use the global timeout.\n- `fetch_timeout` is not accepted on feed creation, and there is no field for it in the web UI's feed edit form.\n- The negative-value error message is a plain English string, not a translated locale key.", "t": 1794463034.667}
{"tool": "_result", "name": "finish", "chars": 55, "t": 1794463034.667}
